  "title": "tine judge VERB --json",
  "description": "Judge assurance (0.89). `classify` runs label judges (label, probability, explicit abstain; a parse failure is an error, never a 0) and ensembles whose members must be independent (copies of one judge count once); with `--key --out` it writes signed `opentine.judge-outcome/1` lines. `agreement` recomputes human and judge-vs-human agreement over a `tine label` queue (judge-vs-consensus Cohen's kappa and multi-rater Krippendorff's alpha, bootstrap intervals; undefined never passes); `validate` signs a judge validation (signed adversarial outcomes plus the floor); `independence` checks judges, monitors and eval items against the candidate's lineage; `injection` lists candidate outputs aimed at their judge (advisory).",
